# breakdown
- In Linux, command options start with dashes, causing cat to interpret leading hyphens as command flags rather than a filename.
- ./ forces cat to recognize the target as a relative file path. Wrapping the full path in quotes handles the spaces within the filename so the shell treats it as a single argument.


# command 
